{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he was not, etc.</b> Since people might come to say <b>he died for his sin</b>, they needed to say: not among the complainers did he die, nor was he in Korah's assembly who incited against the Holy One, blessed be He — but for his sin alone he died, and he did not cause others to sin with him (Sifrei). Rabbi Akiva says: he was the wood-gatherer. Rabbi Shimon says: he was among the trespassers (Shabbat 96)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:57.770438408Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}